    translation: `The gods praised Her in the Śakrādaya Stuti: "You who are Fortune (Śrī) in the dwellings of the virtuous, and misfortune (Alakṣmī) in the houses of the corrupt; You who are discriminating intellect (Buddhi) in the hearts of the wise, unwavering faith (Śraddhā) in the righteous, and modesty (Lajjā) in the noble—to You, O Goddess, we bow! Protect the universe!"`,
